--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-iio-mpu6515-dmp
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_rot_quaternion_scale
+What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_rot_quaternion_sampling_frequency
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.4
+Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
+Description:
+		MPU6515 DMP six-axis quaternion output. The scale is exactly
+		2^-30 and the read-only sampling frequency is 25 Hz. Buffered
+		values are four signed, native-endian 32-bit integers in W, X,
+		Y, Z order, in the firmware's sensor coordinate frame. W is
+		reconstructed as the nonnegative square root of 1-X^2-Y^2-Z^2.
+		This representation does not provide a continuous quaternion
+		sign choice or an absolute magnetic heading.
+
+		Enable in_rot_quaternion in scan_elements to select DMP output.
+		The quaternion scan mask excludes the ordinary raw channels.
+		The optional software timestamp uses the selected IIO clock;
+		batch timestamps are reconstructed at 40 ms intervals ending
+		at the IRQ timestamp. They are not hardware packet timestamps.
+		Use the scan type and index attributes and IIO core alignment
+		rules to interpret the buffer. On the introducing core, the
+		quaternion occupies bytes 0-15, the timestamp bytes 16-23, and
+		the complete timestamped scan is 32 bytes including tail padding.
+
+		DMP operation requires invensense/mpu6515-dmp.bin through the
+		firmware loader. Only the 2943-byte reference image matching
+		CRC32 0xa7e2110d (initial CRC zero) is accepted. Firmware is
+		reloaded and verified on each start; it is not stored in the
+		kernel source. Ordinary raw sampling does not require this file.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/events/in_activity_still_change_falling_en
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.4
+Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
+Description:
+		MPU6515 DMP significant-motion one-shot event. Write 1 to arm
+		using the reference firmware's fixed configuration, or 0 to
+		disable and restore the saved raw-sensor configuration. Reads
+		indicate whether it is armed. A firmware SMD status indication
+		emits an IIO_ACTIVITY / IIO_MOD_STILL change-falling event and
+		disarms it; userspace must explicitly rearm for another event.
+		Pedometer status alone does not emit this event.
+
+		Arming requires the reference firmware described above and
+		is exclusive with raw/quaternion buffered sampling and ordinary
+		accelerometer wake-on-motion. It holds a runtime-PM reference
+		while armed. System suspend may retain the running DMP only
+		when device wakeup is enabled and IRQ wake can be armed. The
+		event timestamp is the host observation time, not a firmware
+		measurement of the physical start of motion. A resume without
+		an SMD indication leaves the one-shot event armed. Configuration
+		changes are rejected while the DMP suspend state is retained.
